    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In the late 1800s, the area’s logging industry relied on wagons hauling lumber down steep grades to Molino box factory in Highland.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Running_Springs%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s first ski resort, Snow Valley Mountain Resort, opened in the 1920s and was the first in the San Bernardino Mountains.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Running_Springs%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Serrano people left mortar holes across the valley, evidence of grinding acorns into meal long before settlers arrived.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
